    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499-a5">

                <pb facs="0568" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg548"/>

                <head>No. 5.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 79.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Kanagawa</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-08-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 19, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to request your excellencies to inform me whether his Majesty
                    the Tycoon approves of the convention made in his behalf, by his <pb facs="0569"
                        n="549" xml:id="pg549"/> ambassadors, with his Majesty the Emperor of
                    France, to open the Inland sea by the removal of the obstructions at Simonoseki,
                    and will carry the same into immediate effect, as such information may have an
                    important influence on my action.</p>
                <p>Should your excellencies not be able to reply to this at once, I desire to have
                    an interview with your excellencies, and should be pleased to have you appoint
                    as early a day as Tuesday for such conference.</p>
                <p>With respect and esteem,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United
                            States in Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Their Excellencies the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministers for Foreign
                            Affairs</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., Yedo.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
